<SiteLayout title="About Ardor" description="Ardor is my personal research system. Ardor Lite publicly showcases selected research from that project." type="about">
<header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">About the project</span><h1>The work is in<br />the research decisions.</h1><p class="lede">Ardor examines whether a plausible market mechanism survives information timing, actual-instrument execution, costs, dependence-aware inference and attribution.</p></header>
<div class="prose"><h2>Independently built and directed</h2><p>{authorship.ownership}</p><p>The concrete work includes clean data access, causal inputs, execution guards, versioned experiments, accounting corrections and retained failed findings. <a href="/engineering/">Inside Ardor</a> connects those boundaries to selected original source operations and bounded synthetic examples.</p><h2>Ardor and Ardor Lite</h2><p>Ardor is my personal research system. Ardor Lite is a public showcase of selected research from that project. Its six cases retain failed, invalid, blocked and discovery-only outcomes with their original distinctions. The reviewed work supports no certified or live strategy.</p><p>Enter through <a href="/">any of the six research questions</a>, or inspect <a href="/research/cases/price-bridge/">Price bridge's separate numerical and rights gates</a>. The <a href="/methods/">synthetic demonstrations</a> explain selected reusable concepts without claiming historical return replication.</p><h2>A concrete research decision</h2><p>In <a href="/research/cases/momentum-v2/">Momentum v2</a>, the monthly long/short spread passed execution stress tests. The separate daily attribution test found negative residual alpha after factor controls, so the research stopped. A favorable intermediate statistic did not become an independent-alpha claim. Ardor Lite preserves both findings and their different questions.</p><h2>Rights and attribution</h2><p>External research, third-party libraries and upstream materials retain their own rights and attribution. See the <a href="/publication/">material-specific notices</a>.</p><h2>Start reading</h2><p><a class="text-link" href="/research/">Explore the research</a></p></div>
</SiteLayout>
